    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply the numerators:**\n   The numerators are \\(1\\) and \\(3\\). Multiplying these together gives:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 3 = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the denominators:**\n   The denominators are \\(5\\) and \\(7\\). Multiplying these together gives:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 7 = 35\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combine the results:**\n   Now, we combine the results of the numerators and denominators to form the new fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 \\times 3}{5 \\times 7} = \\frac{3}{35}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
